0.004090852873345798,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":93.2,"_gate_insider_own":0.0128,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":8.5,"_gate_insider_buying":0.25,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":25.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Insight Enterprises, Inc., together with its subsidiaries, provides information technology, hardware, software, and services in the United States, rest of North America, Europe, Middle East, Africa, and the Asia-Pacific. It offers multicloud solutions that manages and supports cloud and data center platforms, modern networks, and edge technologies; cybersecurity solutions automates and securely connects modern platforms, including networks, security systems, and automation tools; data and artificial intelligence solutions; digital workplace and device solutions; and intelligent application solutions. The company provides software maintenance solutions that offers clients to obtain software upgrades, bug fixes, help desk, and other support services; vendor direct support services contracts; and cloud/software-as-a-service subscription products. In addition, it designs, procures, deploys, implements, and manages solutions that combine hardware, software, and services to help businesses. The company serves construction, esports, financial services, health care and life sciences, manufacturing, retail and restaurant, service providers, small to medium business, and travel and tourism industries. The company was founded in 1988 and is headquartered in Chandler, Arizona.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jack  Azagury | CEO, President & Director","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 14K people. Revenue per employee of $569K ranks in the above the sector median among Technology peers. Each employee generates $19K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Insight Enterprises, Inc. is a mid-cap technology business with a $4.9B market cap on $8.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -8% over the past three years and +4% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 15% against a 9% cost of capital, a 6-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it, and 14% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $279M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 3 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.93\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 3.9\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 3.1% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.2\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Technology peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.24838255977496432},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Technology peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (38% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Antitrust and platform-regulation risk \u2014 the larger the network effect, the larger the regulatory target on its back, and a single consent decree can reset the moat.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"AI disruption of existing software moats \u2014 incumbents with durable margins face commoditisation as AI-native competitors replicate features at a fraction of the R&D cost.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 15% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Valued at a 42% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Insight Enterprises Inc (NSIT) (Q3 2026) Earnings Call Highlights: AI-Driven Demand Fuels 34% ...","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/technology/ai/articles/insight-enterprises-inc-nsit-q3-010120715.html","date":"2026-11-14","timestamp":1794618080.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.202,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Insight Enterprises (NSIT) Looks Fairly Valued Following Microsoft AI Awards","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/tech/nasdaq-nsit/insight-enterprises/news/insight-enterprises-nsit-looks-fairly-valued-following-micro","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794551916.227,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.946,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Comparing Insight Enterprises (NASDAQ:NSIT) and Actelis Networks (NASDAQ:ASNS)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/comparing-insight-en